WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:04.501
-Hey, everybody.

00:00:04.501 --> 00:00:07.434
"It's a little cold outside,
but that doesn't mean

00:00:07.434 --> 00:00:08.901
'Corrections'
aren't heating up."

00:00:08.901 --> 00:00:11.367
Ugh. Baze.

00:00:11.367 --> 00:00:13.133
[ Laughter ]

00:00:15.133 --> 00:00:18.267
George Washington, we said
he wore a powdered wig.

00:00:18.267 --> 00:00:22.501
I was told by a bunch of people,

00:00:22.501 --> 00:00:24.300
George Washington
didn't wear a wig.

00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:27.801
He had red hair
that he powdered.

00:00:27.801 --> 00:00:31.968
And he powdered it
because, in his words,

00:00:31.968 --> 00:00:34.868
"Our allies will
never trust a ginger."

00:00:40.133 --> 00:00:44.767
I said that Donatello,
the Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtle,

00:00:44.767 --> 00:00:46.601
stopped wearing his mask because

00:00:46.601 --> 00:00:48.934
last he checked,
this was America.

00:00:48.934 --> 00:00:53.234
Turtle fans, Mutant Ninja Turtle
fans came out in force

00:00:53.234 --> 00:00:57.601
and said Donatello
was the smartest

00:00:57.601 --> 00:01:00.067
of the Ninja Turtles.

00:01:00.067 --> 00:01:04.100
More likely,
it would be Raphael.

00:01:04.100 --> 00:01:10.534
But in reality, the smart ones
are often the first to reject

00:01:10.534 --> 00:01:13.801
scientific consensus, because
they're smart enough to know

00:01:13.801 --> 00:01:16.801
that will get them
booked on podcasts.

00:01:19.534 --> 00:01:24.534
I am, I will admit, anti-mask.

00:01:24.534 --> 00:01:27.968
Not N95 mask.

00:01:27.968 --> 00:01:30.467
I'm anti

00:01:30.467 --> 00:01:34.601
the Mutant Ninja Turtles
wearing masks.

00:01:34.601 --> 00:01:37.834
Because why?

00:01:37.834 --> 00:01:41.000
Is it a disguise?

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:44.968
Like, if they didn't wear them,

00:01:44.968 --> 00:01:48.167
like, would they be able to
go about their regular life...

00:01:50.167 --> 00:01:53.934
...like, above-ground
as just walking,

00:01:53.934 --> 00:01:57.133
talking turtles?

00:01:57.133 --> 00:01:59.601
Also,

00:01:59.601 --> 00:02:02.601
could you not recognize them,

00:02:02.601 --> 00:02:05.434
'cause this part is covered?

00:02:05.434 --> 00:02:08.501
Here, do a little --
a little experiment.

00:02:13.734 --> 00:02:16.434
Do you -- Do you guys know
it's still me?

00:02:16.434 --> 00:02:19.000
[ Laughter ]

00:02:23.334 --> 00:02:25.767
Many thanks to Eric,
who got a call

00:02:25.767 --> 00:02:28.300
only like 90 minutes ago.

00:02:28.300 --> 00:02:30.100
Yeah.

00:02:30.100 --> 00:02:31.801
"Corrections" is a team effort.

00:02:34.934 --> 00:02:37.133
I said in order to be
a serial killer,

00:02:37.133 --> 00:02:39.033
it has to be three victims.

00:02:39.033 --> 00:02:41.234
This was something I was told.

00:02:41.234 --> 00:02:43.200
Then -- Again,
we often have this.

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:47.601
Someone clarifies the point
on behalf of another jackal.

00:02:47.601 --> 00:02:51.767
The FBI changed and said
it's now two or more.

00:02:51.767 --> 00:02:53.767
So if you got one,
halfway there.

00:02:56.968 --> 00:03:00.634
And then I looked it up,
and there was --

00:03:00.634 --> 00:03:03.467
I read,

00:03:03.467 --> 00:03:07.200
basically a report
from this 2005 FBI symposium

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:09.100
sponsored by the FBI's
National Center

00:03:09.100 --> 00:03:12.634
for the Analysis
of Violent Crime,

00:03:12.634 --> 00:03:18.601
and read about
this reclassification.

00:03:18.601 --> 00:03:21.000
The best thing I read
on the entire --

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:26.367
And this was pages and pages
about the behavioral science

00:03:26.367 --> 00:03:29.200
the FBI uses to catch criminals.

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:30.701
But right at the bottom,

00:03:30.701 --> 00:03:33.267
I read something that just
delighted me to no end.

00:03:33.267 --> 00:03:36.567
It was the agenda for the day.

00:03:36.567 --> 00:03:39.734
And it's said
Monday, August 29, 2005,

00:03:39.734 --> 00:03:43.100
7:30 to 8:00 a.m.,
continental breakfast.

00:03:45.167 --> 00:03:48.868
They're just like us.

00:03:48.868 --> 00:03:52.400
FBI, the F --
They're just like us.

00:03:55.801 --> 00:03:59.167
I know I'm at risk of
getting myself in trouble here,

00:03:59.167 --> 00:04:01.200
but I do

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:04.634
want to say something nice
about serial killers.

00:04:04.634 --> 00:04:07.534
They're the only criminals
who take the time

00:04:07.534 --> 00:04:10.767
to write a note.

00:04:10.767 --> 00:04:14.701
In this day and age,
when we're just moving so fast,

00:04:14.701 --> 00:04:18.200
the fact that they --
Often a handwritten note

00:04:18.200 --> 00:04:21.367
that addresses
the head detective by name.

00:04:24.267 --> 00:04:26.000
You know, in these --
When's the last time

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:31.234
that detective
got a handwritten note?

00:04:31.234 --> 00:04:33.100
Probably when he read one
from his wife

00:04:33.100 --> 00:04:37.000
saying, like,
"I've taken the kids

00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:38.667
to go --
I've taken the kid to my mom's.

00:04:38.667 --> 00:04:42.734
You love your job more than them
anyway," you know?

00:04:42.734 --> 00:04:45.033
I guess kidnappers,
but their notes are like,

00:04:45.033 --> 00:04:48.234
"Do this!
Leave it here! Don't --"

00:04:48.234 --> 00:04:51.400
Kidnappers notes are --

00:04:51.400 --> 00:04:53.934
Arsonists

00:04:53.934 --> 00:04:56.567
love to tell you they left one.

00:04:56.567 --> 00:04:58.667
[ Laughter ]

00:05:03.634 --> 00:05:07.434
Someti-- I mean, they sometimes
even build a little code,

00:05:07.434 --> 00:05:11.267
serial killers,
for you to solve.

00:05:11.267 --> 00:05:13.434
We didn't always have Wordle.

00:05:13.434 --> 00:05:15.167
[ Laughter ]

00:05:18.200 --> 00:05:20.934
I said Prince Andrew
rescinded his title.

00:05:20.934 --> 00:05:24.834
It was revoked by the Queen.

00:05:24.834 --> 00:05:27.901
He didn't rescind his title.

00:05:27.901 --> 00:05:30.834
She took it away. And I guess

00:05:30.834 --> 00:05:33.167
it took away his patronages.

00:05:33.167 --> 00:05:34.901
I don't know what any of this
means. His --

00:05:34.901 --> 00:05:37.000
Anyway, they're distancing --

00:05:37.000 --> 00:05:41.234
He's not allowed to say
His Royal Highness anymore,

00:05:41.234 --> 00:05:42.868
because they're
distancing themselves.

00:05:42.868 --> 00:05:45.234
The royal family,
from what I've read,

00:05:45.234 --> 00:05:48.067
is distancing themselves
from Prince Andrew.

00:05:48.067 --> 00:05:52.000
The problem's always going to be
the prince in his name...

00:05:55.334 --> 00:05:59.167
...as far as
the distancing goes.

00:05:59.167 --> 00:06:02.701
What they should do
is give him --

00:06:02.701 --> 00:06:04.601
If they made him wear
one of these --

00:06:11.767 --> 00:06:13.767
We said a single piece
of confetti

00:06:13.767 --> 00:06:16.734
was called a confettum.

00:06:16.734 --> 00:06:19.467
That was a comedy way
of saying it.

00:06:19.467 --> 00:06:22.067
I mean, man, I can't believe
how many of you knew

00:06:22.067 --> 00:06:24.534
it was called a confetto.

00:06:24.534 --> 00:06:26.834
But did you know Confetto

00:06:26.834 --> 00:06:30.334
was also the fifth
Mutant Ninja Turtle?

00:06:34.033 --> 00:06:37.033
Who loved to party.

00:06:37.033 --> 00:06:38.501
Little bit too hard.

00:06:41.434 --> 00:06:45.033
This isn't a correction

00:06:45.033 --> 00:06:48.334
as much as a clarification.

00:06:48.334 --> 00:06:50.901
Last night was a great night.
David Letterman,

00:06:50.901 --> 00:06:54.100
the David Letterman,
was sitting right here.

00:06:54.100 --> 00:06:56.133
Incredible to get
to talk to him.

00:06:56.133 --> 00:07:00.601
And he told a wonderful story
about when zookeeper Jack Hanna,

00:07:00.601 --> 00:07:04.000
a frequent guest on his show,

00:07:04.000 --> 00:07:06.901
was bitten by a beaver
on his hand

00:07:06.901 --> 00:07:10.200
and had to be taken
to a New York City E.R.

00:07:10.200 --> 00:07:12.534
because of how

00:07:12.534 --> 00:07:14.467
much blood

00:07:14.467 --> 00:07:16.133
came out when the beaver
bit him. And the reason

00:07:16.133 --> 00:07:17.767
I bring this up --
This is the clarification.

00:07:17.767 --> 00:07:19.067
At one point,
David Letterman said,

00:07:19.067 --> 00:07:21.133
"You must have an animal guy,"
and I said I didn't.

00:07:21.133 --> 00:07:23.868
And he said, "Oh, my God.
You got to get an animal guy."

00:07:23.868 --> 00:07:27.167
Here's the thing. We had
an animal guy on this show.

00:07:27.167 --> 00:07:29.501
Lovely. But there was a moment
on this show,

00:07:29.501 --> 00:07:31.701
the last time
we had animals on the show,

00:07:31.701 --> 00:07:33.601
we had a sloth.

00:07:33.601 --> 00:07:36.467
And we were over there,
and at one point --

00:07:36.467 --> 00:07:37.834
The audience loved it.

00:07:37.834 --> 00:07:41.367
I mean, being in the same room
as a sloth?

00:07:43.734 --> 00:07:48.801
But at one point, I made
eye contact with the sloth,

00:07:48.801 --> 00:07:52.467
who very much had
an expression that said,

00:07:52.467 --> 00:07:55.934
"I don't want to be here."

00:07:55.934 --> 00:07:57.400
And I know that expr--

00:07:57.400 --> 00:07:59.968
I've seen it on numerous guests.

00:07:59.968 --> 00:08:01.767
[ Laughter ]

00:08:05.968 --> 00:08:08.634
But they choose to be here.

00:08:08.634 --> 00:08:10.200
That is the difference.

00:08:10.200 --> 00:08:12.300
The sloth --

00:08:12.300 --> 00:08:15.033
You know, people come here.
they're plugging a project.

00:08:15.033 --> 00:08:17.467
What's the sloth --

00:08:17.467 --> 00:08:21.868
I don't think the sloth cares
how many people come to the zoo,

00:08:21.868 --> 00:08:25.367
I mean, unless they're
sloth liberators.

00:08:25.367 --> 00:08:28.734
So I, you know, I made --
And for a sloth

00:08:28.734 --> 00:08:31.067
to make this expression to me,

00:08:31.067 --> 00:08:36.033
it required so much effort,
'cause his head was here

00:08:36.033 --> 00:08:38.534
and it had to come
all the way over here.

00:08:38.534 --> 00:08:40.601
The whole segment,

00:08:40.601 --> 00:08:43.267
which was like six minutes,
it was just --

00:08:48.167 --> 00:08:51.167
And you could just -- The sweat

00:08:51.167 --> 00:08:52.834
coming down the temples
of the cloth,

00:08:52.834 --> 00:08:55.501
hoping that it would make
eye contact

00:08:55.501 --> 00:08:57.467
before the end of the segment.
And it did.

00:08:57.467 --> 00:09:01.167
And so since that day,
I just thought to myself,

00:09:01.167 --> 00:09:05.300
all things being equal,
I don't --

00:09:05.300 --> 00:09:10.133
I don't want an animal
that doesn't want to be here

00:09:10.133 --> 00:09:12.434
to be here. Also,

00:09:12.434 --> 00:09:14.267
somebody else screwed up.

00:09:14.267 --> 00:09:17.067
They had told the sloth
he was going to be on "Fallon."

00:09:17.067 --> 00:09:19.100
[ Laughter ]

00:09:19.100 --> 00:09:20.701
So I think it was twofold.

00:09:24.701 --> 00:09:28.133
Oh. I didn't know if I was going
to tell you guys or not,

00:09:28.133 --> 00:09:30.167
but I'm wearing a new jacket.

00:09:30.167 --> 00:09:32.601
[ Laughter ]

00:09:34.734 --> 00:09:36.934
[ Sighs ] Long story.

00:09:36.934 --> 00:09:38.334
I'll tell it 'cause I'm assuming

00:09:38.334 --> 00:09:41.734
everyone who watches
"Corrections" are first-timers.

00:09:41.734 --> 00:09:45.234
[ Laughter ]

00:09:45.234 --> 00:09:47.634
Talked about Olive Garden.

00:09:47.634 --> 00:09:50.033
"When you're here,
you're family."

00:09:50.033 --> 00:09:51.834
It turns out Jimmy Fallon
got the rights

00:09:51.834 --> 00:09:53.267
to "When you're here,
you're family."

00:09:53.267 --> 00:09:54.968
I was angry at NBC.

00:09:54.968 --> 00:09:58.601
They then got me the rights to

00:09:58.601 --> 00:10:01.501
"Nobody out-pizzas the Hut"

00:10:01.501 --> 00:10:04.868
for me to use on the show.

00:10:04.868 --> 00:10:07.434
That was a fib.

00:10:07.434 --> 00:10:12.300
I was fibbing. I didn't -- I
didn't really get the rights to

00:10:12.300 --> 00:10:14.334
But we did mention pizza.

00:10:14.334 --> 00:10:16.367
And the good people
at Pizza Hut,

00:10:16.367 --> 00:10:17.868
they reached out,

00:10:17.868 --> 00:10:22.334
and they sent pizza
for the crew today.

00:10:22.334 --> 00:10:23.734
And I just want
to thank them for that.

00:10:23.734 --> 00:10:26.167
That was such
a very nice gesture.

00:10:26.167 --> 00:10:28.567
And this jacket.

00:10:28.567 --> 00:10:31.601
And I had no intention
of wearing the jacket out here,

00:10:31.601 --> 00:10:33.801
but the crew,

00:10:33.801 --> 00:10:38.067
collectively --
They're a very tight-knit bunch.

00:10:38.067 --> 00:10:40.467
That's why we nicknamed them
"the crew."

00:10:40.467 --> 00:10:42.467
[ Laughter ]

00:10:45.634 --> 00:10:48.667
So, the crew came over to me
collectively and said,

00:10:48.667 --> 00:10:51.567
"Well, you going to
wear the jacket?"

00:10:51.567 --> 00:10:54.467
I said, "No, I'm -- I'm not
going to wear the jacket."

00:10:54.467 --> 00:10:56.968
They said,
"Well, uh, they sent pizza."

00:10:56.968 --> 00:10:59.534
[ Laughter ]

00:10:59.534 --> 00:11:02.701
"Might be nice
to wear the jacket."

00:11:02.701 --> 00:11:04.834
And I said, "Yeah,
but they already sent the pizza.

00:11:04.834 --> 00:11:06.300
They're not going to --

00:11:06.300 --> 00:11:08.801
If I wear the jacket, they're
not going to send more pizza.

00:11:08.801 --> 00:11:10.567
It's a one-time thing."
And they said,

00:11:10.567 --> 00:11:12.367
"Put on the jacket."

00:11:12.367 --> 00:11:15.133
[ Laughter ]

00:11:15.133 --> 00:11:18.434
So I --

00:11:18.434 --> 00:11:21.534
Because the crew is --

00:11:21.534 --> 00:11:24.334
It's -- They're not menacing.
What's the word?

00:11:24.334 --> 00:11:26.234
Oh, ye-- Oh, it is menacing.

00:11:26.234 --> 00:11:27.834
[ Laughter ]

00:11:29.901 --> 00:11:33.901
But my fear was, of course,
you know, I'd wear the jacket,

00:11:33.901 --> 00:11:36.501
and it would just be,
you know --

00:11:36.501 --> 00:11:39.767
Pizza Hut could clip it. This
would be on buses, you know.

00:11:39.767 --> 00:11:41.701
'Cause, again, was no --

00:11:41.701 --> 00:11:44.267
No money has changed hands here.

00:11:44.267 --> 00:11:47.934
Just pizzas and a jacket.

00:11:47.934 --> 00:11:49.767
And a handful of hats.

00:11:52.067 --> 00:11:55.067
So I did -- I thought fast
right before we came on,

00:11:55.067 --> 00:11:56.968
and I have -- You'll notice --

00:11:56.968 --> 00:11:58.300
I wanted to make it impossible

00:11:58.300 --> 00:12:00.467
for them to use this
as free advertising,

00:12:00.467 --> 00:12:05.334
so I've changed it
to Pizza Hatz.

00:12:05.334 --> 00:12:08.567
And I know a lot of you
are going to scramble now

00:12:08.567 --> 00:12:10.701
to try to buy

00:12:10.701 --> 00:12:12.934
that domain name. Too late.

00:12:15.534 --> 00:12:17.968
Too late. Pizzahatz.com --

00:12:17.968 --> 00:12:21.567
The Z's there 'cause Pizza Hats
with a "S" was taken.

00:12:23.734 --> 00:12:26.234
Not in use.

00:12:26.234 --> 00:12:31.200
Pizzahatz.com is just on sale --

00:12:31.200 --> 00:12:35.267
Wait for it -- for $1,600.

00:12:35.267 --> 00:12:37.400
Can you imagine?

00:12:37.400 --> 00:12:39.367
But pizzahatz.com --

00:12:39.367 --> 00:12:42.400
Now, again, there's one thing

00:12:42.400 --> 00:12:45.601
I'm terrified about. I...

00:12:45.601 --> 00:12:48.501
told my assistant Chelsea,

00:12:48.501 --> 00:12:52.000
"You got to go buy pizzahatz.com
right now."

00:12:52.000 --> 00:12:55.601
And heaven forbid she forgets,
because by the time --

00:12:55.601 --> 00:12:56.968
Again, there's going to be --

00:12:56.968 --> 00:13:00.467
If the Internet is slow
when you're watching this,

00:13:00.467 --> 00:13:02.300
that's 'cause
everybody's racing...

00:13:04.634 --> 00:13:05.734
...to try to buy pizzaha--

00:13:05.734 --> 00:13:07.667
And of course,
the second fear --

00:13:07.667 --> 00:13:08.901
And you know Chelsea.
I know Chelsea --

00:13:08.901 --> 00:13:11.367
is that she's going to --

00:13:11.367 --> 00:13:13.801
She's going to buy it

00:13:13.801 --> 00:13:16.067
and then try to get
the 1,600 bucks out of me.

00:13:19.634 --> 00:13:21.868
And also, I want to say --
This is the last thing I'll say.

00:13:21.868 --> 00:13:23.667
To, again, good people
at Pizza Hut

00:13:23.667 --> 00:13:25.734
who are very kind
and sent pizzas and hats

00:13:25.734 --> 00:13:28.400
and no -- Is it "renumeration"?
Am I saying that right?

00:13:28.400 --> 00:13:29.667
Baze, is that right?

00:13:29.667 --> 00:13:32.667
"Renumeration"? Okay.
Went out on a limb.

00:13:32.667 --> 00:13:34.834
Very -- Very risky
to try a new word

00:13:34.834 --> 00:13:36.701
in the middle of "Corrections."

00:13:42.767 --> 00:13:44.367
So, anyway,

00:13:44.367 --> 00:13:48.267
I want to say -- And I've been
told by our legal team

00:13:48.267 --> 00:13:50.601
that if I say, "You are not --

00:13:50.601 --> 00:13:53.334
Pizza Hut, you're not to use
a photo of me in this jacket

00:13:53.334 --> 00:13:57.501
without the express
written consent

00:13:57.501 --> 00:13:59.934
of Major League Baseball."

00:13:59.934 --> 00:14:02.834
I don't know why it's them,

00:14:02.834 --> 00:14:05.167
but I guess
they're just the best at it.

00:14:05.167 --> 00:14:09.267
I think they have all the forms
in just, like, a template.

00:14:09.267 --> 00:14:14.801
They're very good
at express written consent.

00:14:14.801 --> 00:14:17.667
It's why the Phillie Phanatic's
never been MeToo'd.

00:14:20.100 --> 00:14:21.567
You think?

00:14:25.501 --> 00:14:26.934
A lot of you noticed
last week --

00:14:26.934 --> 00:14:30.567
I usually hold up a card
at the end.

00:14:30.567 --> 00:14:33.801
I didn't do that last week.

00:14:33.801 --> 00:14:35.934
And then I had one,

00:14:35.934 --> 00:14:39.033
and then I just left it
in my dressing room.

00:14:39.033 --> 00:14:42.501
And I thought about it
about a minute ago.

00:14:42.501 --> 00:14:44.367
Too late.

00:14:44.367 --> 00:14:46.734
These are one-take
"Corrections," bros.

00:14:46.734 --> 00:14:48.534
Ladies.

